                        "form": "му́торны"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "5ab7b6f7-351e-434d-baae-8158a7bec79d",
                        "entry_id": "afc911f9-6b69-3314-b3d8-af1883caf049",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "му́торнее"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "101599ef-c4dd-4500-897b-156b725a8bf1",
                        "entry_id": "afc911f9-6b69-3314-b3d8-af1883caf049",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "му́торней"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6bfa00b0-70b7-3307-a141-d421320b389f",
                        "entry_id": "afc911f9-6b69-3314-b3d8-af1883caf049",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. вызывающий тошноту, подташнивание"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bbf1bb4-3b23-4e59-9ab1-6e4a3a7fd938",
                                "sense_id": "6bfa00b0-70b7-3307-a141-d421320b389f",
                                "text": "А самолёт и не качало, он шёл, как автобус по бетонке, но всё равно желудок наливался муторной тяжестью, и сердце словно повисало в пустоте."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3dd1c904-a2d8-3b37-92b0-5328124a10f2",
                        "entry_id": "afc911f9-6b69-3314-b3d8-af1883caf049",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., разг. неприятный и тоскливый, тревожный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "415c756a-5fa5-4532-b4e0-57137c331bf0",
                                "sense_id": "3dd1c904-a2d8-3b37-92b0-5328124a10f2",
                                "text": "Особенно трудно было хозяйке с заготовкой рыбы впрок: для засолки не хватало посуды, а сушить на плите, без всяких приспособлений — муторное дело, плита раскалена, рыба на ней не сохнет, а горит."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2e48c80-7514-428d-868b-2e829fbe2841",
                                "sense_id": "3dd1c904-a2d8-3b37-92b0-5328124a10f2",
                                "text": "Это была муторная, напряжённая, жуткая ночь. Дину всю трясло."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9fb35da9-1ecf-42d5-87da-5c84e4c84f30",
                        "source_entry_id": "afc911f9-6b69-3314-b3d8-af1883caf049",
                        "target_lang_word": "disagreeable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disagreeable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6ac6799-ebc2-32d0-b964-3f8a64717243",
                                        "entry_id": "242afbdc-3756-3c4e-b903-169f5ffff361",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Causing repugnance; unpleasant to the feelings or senses; displeasing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6405923-9888-4748-a879-065167babd9b",
                                                "sense_id": "d6ac6799-ebc2-32d0-b964-3f8a64717243",
                                                "text": "disagreeable weather"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf4671fa-a421-4f67-93ca-8c3b61bf9335",
                                                "sense_id": "d6ac6799-ebc2-32d0-b964-3f8a64717243",
                                                "text": "disagreeable person"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f5a3be0-3587-4ee4-906d-c2567c72e413",
                                                "sense_id": "d6ac6799-ebc2-32d0-b964-3f8a64717243",
                                                "text": "disagreeable attitude"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c0d5ca6-fce6-4757-b244-9c7c910e26cc",
                                                "sense_id": "d6ac6799-ebc2-32d0-b964-3f8a64717243",
                                                "text": "disagreeable taste"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "006e7bc9-b7a7-4fee-bfc1-d0de164a65d9",
                                                "sense_id": "d6ac6799-ebc2-32d0-b964-3f8a64717243",
                                                "text": "That which is disagreeable to one is many times agreeable to another, or disagreeable in a less degree."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b698512-995f-39dd-8a9a-7764bff119b3",
                                        "entry_id": "242afbdc-3756-3c4e-b903-169f5ffff361",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not suitable; that does not conform or fit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f265f838-8212-48bb-ae9d-69768706c1ff",
                                                "sense_id": "1b698512-995f-39dd-8a9a-7764bff119b3",
                                                "text": "The first author I shall cite is Justin Martyr, who is not only silent about infant-baptism, as are all the fathers before him, but says what is inconsistent with it; for the reason he assigns, as what he had received from the apostles themselves, why baptism was instituted, is altogether incompatible and disagreeable thereunto."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f900050-6298-4686-b296-0e18f6b01e5c",
                                                "sense_id": "1b698512-995f-39dd-8a9a-7764bff119b3",
                                                "text": "Now to say, that justice is opposed to forgiveness, when by forgiveness we mean the entire cure of sin and misery; is to say that justice chooses that to remain forever, which is perfectly disagreeable to itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e64630e-f2f1-4a2e-b93f-196782a318ab",
                                                "sense_id": "1b698512-995f-39dd-8a9a-7764bff119b3",
                                                "text": "We cannot but judge it disagreeable with the spirit and principles of the gospel, and an encroachment upon the divine prerogative and the undoubted rights of mankind, to punish any for their conscientious and peaceable dissent from the established way of religion, while they are not justly chargeable with any immorality, or what is plainly destructive of civil society."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1c9ba03-6ac3-450a-82b9-a926b6c1dead",
                                                "sense_id": "1b698512-995f-39dd-8a9a-7764bff119b3",
                                                "text": "and that this Nation that is invested in a Law particular and municipal, which doth in no wise so much as challenge or claim any derivation from, or dependency of the Civil Law, but is altogether different and disagreeable thereunto in its proceedings, and oftentimes in its determinations, and hath no foundation or grounds whereon the decisions of Sea controversies can be built, should without the knowledge and practise of these Civil and Maritime Laws deal and trade with such as do live under them, and are guided by them?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disagreeable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f111fee-bb62-3bb3-8c82-e9f316134332",
                                        "entry_id": "581cc476-883b-3b9c-8d51-895360975d83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something or someone displeasing; anything that is disagreeable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebd64d78-63a4-45a3-b007-a1776876fc77",
                                                "sense_id": "3f111fee-bb62-3bb3-8c82-e9f316134332",
                                                "text": "The disagreeables of travelling are necessary evils, to be encountered for the sake of the agreeables of resting and looking round you."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eabcd507-b380-41b0-ba13-756cff6b3219",
                        "source_entry_id": "afc911f9-6b69-3314-b3d8-af1883caf049",
                        "target_lang_word": "dreary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dreary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c0e40cf-8e3d-35ae-93ac-b817ffd3964c",
                                        "entry_id": "5763fe1e-67a2-3295-8a69-4cb8ae89c308",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Drab; dark, colorless, or cheerless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "189ed187-eeb7-4151-900f-3fb7e6d880f9",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0e40cf-8e3d-35ae-93ac-b817ffd3964c",
                                                "text": "It had rained for three days straight, and the dreary weather dragged the townspeople's spirits down."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d43e4031-df69-4106-8933-3cf14e8d8891",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0e40cf-8e3d-35ae-93ac-b817ffd3964c",
                                                "text": "Once upon a midnight dreary, while I pondered, weak and weary..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bf4b754-6a29-471c-9d21-b0738f11f722",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0e40cf-8e3d-35ae-93ac-b817ffd3964c",
                                                "text": "It was on a dreary night of November, that I beheld the accomplishment of my toils."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9e6bbab-4b62-48e3-b5df-d5dcc47fd7f3",
                                                "sense_id": "7c0e40cf-8e3d-35ae-93ac-b817ffd3964c",
                                                "text": "The train is booked to stop at Jiza for only three minutes, but more often than not twenty minutes or more are spent on shunting before it sets off again on what must be one of the most dreary journeys in the world."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa54c26d-de41-32ef-99f9-1e84e2c1b35f",
                                        "entry_id": "5763fe1e-67a2-3295-8a69-4cb8ae89c308",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Grievous, dire; appalling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "dreary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "600332de-69bf-344c-8433-c2bafa2d2f5e",
                                        "entry_id": "2b2f17a8-306d-3524-9385-cc562881be35",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dreary person or thing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28cc060f-393b-4782-ba8f-6614799f669a",
                                                "sense_id": "600332de-69bf-344c-8433-c2bafa2d2f5e",
                                                "text": "In the glow of this project Steele manages to forget altogether the parade of donnish and scholastic drearies, the barricades of schoolbooks, texts, examinations with which he has dealt so faithfully."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a003a57-83c3-4323-808b-d0148114f956",
                                                "sense_id": "600332de-69bf-344c-8433-c2bafa2d2f5e",
                                                "text": "2018, Tibor Fischer, The Thought Gang\nI'm taking it all down. The trivialities. The ramblings. The drearies. The trites."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e3f5d29a-48d9-4bbe-8b81-691801f2a282",
                        "source_entry_id": "afc911f9-6b69-3314-b3d8-af1883caf049",
                        "target_lang_word": "sombre",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sombre",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e316e64-b1a8-300c-98e2-f9c0211b0f63",
                                        "entry_id": "5865c01d-e16f-3c91-911d-a393f7e66701",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dark; gloomy; shadowy, dimly lit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a41bc1ea-4c86-40e6-8e0a-78ec17129100",
                                                "sense_id": "5e316e64-b1a8-300c-98e2-f9c0211b0f63",
                                                "text": "The lady led him into a sombre hallway and disappeared. A moment later the windowless chamber was illuminated by the entry of a heavenly creature emitting a radiance prone to pierce the heart of any youth exposed to it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13428f6a-60a2-41ce-bb62-d2b74aa408c2",
                                                "sense_id": "5e316e64-b1a8-300c-98e2-f9c0211b0f63",
                                                "text": "All three parallel valleys of the Llynvi, Garw and Ogmore are much the same in physical character: the lower reaches are wooded and not unattractive, but as the railway climbs on ever-steepening grades, the hills on either hand grow barer and closer together, while in all respects the scene becomes more sombre, with the terraced, slate-roofed colliery towns and the road, railway and river all struggling for space in the narrowing defiles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e21bb46b-de91-3c5d-bbbc-143efd01e745",
                                        "entry_id": "5865c01d-e16f-3c91-911d-a393f7e66701",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dull or dark in colour or brightness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96e366b9-251e-45b7-9400-c9cba7aa56b0",
                                                "sense_id": "e21bb46b-de91-3c5d-bbbc-143efd01e745",
                                                "text": "His tall and slender figure, dressed in sombre black, his hair of that peculiar reddish auburn so rarely seen, his flashing black eyes, in which a fitful fire seemed for ever burning; all combined to give something almost of a demoniac air ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba790717-36a1-3f25-90c7-b8997c267eea",
                                        "entry_id": "5865c01d-e16f-3c91-911d-a393f7e66701",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Melancholic, gloomy, dreary, dismal; grim."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c998d29a-f474-4c22-b78f-dc7404fb0cde",
                                                "sense_id": "ba790717-36a1-3f25-90c7-b8997c267eea",
                                                "text": "The dinner was silent and sombre; happily it was also short."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fc22815-3f7b-4a08-b7b5-1f4f8d324e9b",
                                                "sense_id": "ba790717-36a1-3f25-90c7-b8997c267eea",
                                                "text": "It was a wonder that he had not been a victim of the ferocious and summary executions which marked the course of that tyranny; for Guzman had ruled the country with the sombre imbecility of political fanaticism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "899469fb-8eec-4e4e-ad06-854ba77616f1",
                                                "sense_id": "ba790717-36a1-3f25-90c7-b8997c267eea",
                                                "text": "A sombre mood, very sombre in fact, thought Hennessey, as he stood against the wall observing the procedure for the police. He had not known a mood more sombre to have previously descended on the room."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79fae494-27cf-3aff-8958-2d20bcdf71ad",
                                        "entry_id": "5865c01d-e16f-3c91-911d-a393f7e66701",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Grave; extremely serious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "632a2409-09ae-4dd2-8c4b-636652c72443",
                                                "sense_id": "79fae494-27cf-3aff-8958-2d20bcdf71ad",
                                                "text": "a sombre situation"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
